we are used to heat here in southern  nevada of course but  long-term heat waves with these kind of  record temperatures  that's unusual and it's also dangerous  bianca holman spoke with the national  weather service with some insight  and some tips to try and stay cool  bianca  yeah so staying out of the sun and  staying hydrated is something we're used  to  living here in las vegas and in southern  nevada but experiencing these hot  temperatures for  several days well that's something we're  not used to we were able to check in  with the national weather service and  they say  that there's nothing typical about our  temperatures this week  there are records that may be broken  with temperatures running 10 to 15  degrees above normal  in 2013 a heat wave in southern nevada  had 30 fatalities and more than 350 heat  related injuries  this heat is serious and officials want  everyone to stay safe through this  extended heat wave  it's actually very unusual and one of  the questions we get a lot is  why do we worry about the heat it's the  summer in the desert that's true it does  get warmer at this time but not to this  fast and doesn't last this long  and we're talking about record  temperatures being broken not just in  one site we're talking about  over 40 different locations that might  be seeing record-breaking temperatures  and not for one day  possibly five six or even seven days so  this is  quite a bit uncommon this is not typical  desert southwest heat  and so you might think hitting the lake  will cool you off but that could be  dangerous as well  the water may be cooler but the land  around the lake is hotter than in the  city and you can easily experience  hypothermia heat streak  heat stroke or heat exhaustion and of  course another reminder when it comes to  our vehicles  they say put a something very important  maybe like your purse or your wallet in  the back seat so that you don't forget  your child  or your pet heat related deaths are very  very serious  and they can happen in a matter of  minutes bianca holman 8 news now
 

